A||N||10||Haze_Performance||Aux. Gauge Cluster Question||||7||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||10-02-2000||04:21 PM||||Yesterday I installed a 120mph speedo cluster in my 85 Coupe. I would like to also put it the Aux. gauges. How do I hook them up? Where do I plug in the wires?<P><BR>TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Tigger||10-02-2000||04:36 PM||||Haze,<P>Was that a plug and play mod?<P>I've been thinking of adding one to mine if I run across a 120 mph speedo.  Mine is an 84 SE by the way.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Carrolles||10-02-2000||06:00 PM||||It is not Plug'N'Play for the 85.  The Aux. gauges weren't offered until 86.  You'll have to splice into the wiring harness for the instrument panel.<P>See the following link for advice from MonkeyMan<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||10-02-2000||07:09 PM||||Is the spedo & tach plug'n play? what happens to the voltmeter? I to have a 84' SE||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||10-02-2000||07:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Xtreme Fiero's:<BR><B>Is the spedo & tach plug'n play? what happens to the voltmeter? I to have a 84' SE</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Speedo, Temp & Fuel work perfect. The tach needs to ajusted from V6 to I4. (I didnt do that yet)<P>The 120mph is MUCH nicer than that dark 84/85 cluster.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||10-02-2000||07:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Carrolles:<BR><B>It is not Plug'N'Play for the 85.  The Aux. gauges weren't offered until 86.  You'll have to splice into the wiring harness for the instrument panel.<P>See the following link for advice from MonkeyMan<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A>  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the link.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000006||batboy||10-02-2000||08:05 PM||||Here are some links for adding the ralley gauge pod. This is a write up I did for the forum after I did mine. The first one is the same as what Haze has in his post.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> <P>This next link is a Forum topic about differences in the 1984 Fieros which have a couple quirks compared to the rest of the model years.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002517.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002517.html</A> <P>DaRKLoRD also has my same gauge article that he polished up to make it look pretty and then put it on his webpage. Go to the below link. Navigate to the "Modifications" page. Then go to the "Interiors" page. Finally click on the gauge pod mod link.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carrolles||10-02-2000||11:25 PM||||Batboy,<P>Sorry I mistakenly gave the credit for the excellent write-up to Monkey.  I was trying to find the link before our server shut down for the day and got in a rush.<P>Again my appologies and thanks again for the excellent article.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||10-03-2000||06:52 AM||||  BatBoy and Carrolles, even if you install the entire Speedo Tach cluster itself, do you still have to splice into the harness for the aux guages? I was under the impression that with the entire unit it was plug and play. LMK<P>  Thanks, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000009||batboy||10-03-2000||07:38 AM||||Nope, the aux gauges (ralley pod) have a separate harness if it was factory installed. The 1984 and 1985 Fieros do not even have this extra ralley gauge harness since it was not offered as an option at that time. The instrument cluster (speedo, tach, etc.) is plug and play across the years, but putting in a 120 MPH Fiero cluster will not make the ralley gauge pod automatically plug and play, unless you have a later model Fiero that already has the unused gauge harness tucked away. If not, you just splice in just like I explained in that article.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fotofrank||10-03-2000||01:38 PM||||I have an '84 SE with the 120 spedo/tach and gas/temp gauges. I also installed the rally pod. The 4 main gauges just plug in where the old gagues are(pull one out plug on in).<BR>The rally gauges are a pit harder for an '84.<BR>None or, almost none of the wiring in an '84 is like the rest of the modle year Fieros. The CD put out by Popular Mechanics, for car repair ,is the best source for wireing I have seen . It does not include or mix wireing from different years. (got mine at K-Mart).<BR>To use the oil presure gauge in a '84 the oil sensor must be replaced with one from a V6 or '85 or later I4. The '84 oil sensor is a simple on/off switch. Thereforwe it does not read oil presure,just turns a light on or off. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||10
